{"skill":{"slug":"x0x","displayName":"x0x"},"version":{"version":"0.48.1","createdAt":1792301029729,"changelog":"Update x0x to v0.48.1.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":29490,"sha256":"6875510c1d3a6d0b4b6a3080a4c348cc8960b2fb89bd4347d6bada9dcc833432","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2489,"sha256":"78b854b84d9dc7dc07202ee3a511c001149468fc62acfb37f339065b1d8f00b0","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1792301695759,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f741b680841c914de3f8b1977b753c8afafa36f672f8b955ce29c346504f64ba","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f741b680841c914de3f8b1977b753c8afafa36f672f8b955ce29c346504f64ba","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1792301209689},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":63,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1792301695759},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is mostly coherent for an agent networking daemon, but it deserves Review because it combines persistent installation, bearer-token daemon control, remote execution, and self-update authority.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network transmission, local identity keys, durable API tokens, and data replication are expected for this product class and are substantially disclosed; users must still treat gossip and ordinary stores as non-private and keep the API loopback-only.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Install metadata and Option A download mutable latest GitHub release archives into ~/.local/bin without checksums in the artifact; Option B runs a raw branch shell installer that explicitly lacks GPG verification and automatically starts or stops the daemon.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact does not contain prompt hijacking or hidden evaluator instructions; it discloses important limits such as public gossip, plaintext scratch stores, human consent for owner-key creation, and loopback API defaults, but it also teaches raw bearer-token REST control.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill installs persistent binaries and a daemon, reads local api-token material, documents remote exec and tailnet surfaces, and exposes an authenticated POST /upgrade/apply self-update path without a clear human approval gate in the skill text.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is broad peer-to-peer networking for AI agents, and the documented messaging, sync, stores, file transfer, tailnet, remote exec, and update capabilities are generally aligned with that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable running a persistent networking daemon for agents. Prefer a verified or checksum-pinned install path, avoid the raw shell installer unless you have reviewed and authorized it, keep the API bound to loopback, protect the durable token, and require explicit human approval for self-update, remote exec, autostart, and any non-local API exposure.","findings":"[TM1] expected: The DELETE /sync/devices/:machine_id example is an owner-device revocation command, not evidence of unsafe parameter abuse by itself; it is purpose-aligned and disclosed.\n[RA1] expected: Self-update is documented rather than hidden, but it remains a material Review concern because an agent with the durable token could invoke daemon-side update application.\n[RA2] expected: Persistent installation in ~/.local/bin is expected for a CLI/daemon, but the artifact does not provide integrity checks for the recommended binary download path.\n[E1] expected: The remote shell installer finding is better understood as supply-chain and automatic-daemon-start risk, not data exfiltration; the artifact itself discloses the missing GPG verification.\n[E1] expected: The /events curl example targets the selected x0x API and is normal event streaming for this skill; it is not artifact-backed exfiltration on its own.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1792301695759}}}}}